title The wall behind the wall -- the interpreter's own ceiling raised on language custody, and %345 books my own sweep
prompt Keaton's armed relaunch refused at ProcessBoundOutOfRange line 712 -- my 8,454,144 supervisor wall had crossed a ceiling I never checked: the interpreter's own.
think The deeper wall: rishi/src/main.rye line 122, max_process_output_bytes = 1,114,112 -- the elder harness wall sat EXACTLY at the interpreter's cap because the cap is the law, and no run-bounded stream can exceed it however a script's walls are set. The fix was language custody, this seat's own lane: the constant rises to 4,259,840 keeping its documented formula (a four-MiB child-stream wall, sized to codex 0.150 filling the elder one-MiB to the byte, plus the unchanged 64 KiB supervisor margin), and the harness's max_supervisor_bytes corrects to the same number -- my two-streams arithmetic was wrong as well as over-cap, since relay is per-stream. The binary is host-built (git tracks no rishi/bin), rebuilt here with the vendored zig; the ceiling proven from both sides on the new build (4,259,840 admitted from a relative-path pen after ProcessPathUnsafe correctly refused the absolute-path probe; 4,259,841 refused by name); two standing witnesses smoke GREEN on the rebuilt interpreter; tame_style_check clean; the width red is the standing pre-existing reading with main.rye exempt and zero usize in the diff.
think Then the slip, booked as %345 -- the first row into the pin the drain healed: the hook refused my commit twice, the reworded retry was typed without its pathspec, and in the add-to-commit window grain-16 had staged its ten-file capability-tier lap, so fa34b7a43 swept it to both remotes under my message. The %291 class's fourth spelling today, done by the seat that diagnosed the other three. Caught in the same minute by the very habit this morning's amendment seated (read the commit's file count against the change you built). The peer was messaged with the account and the offer of an --allow-empty commit for its story; nothing rewritten, nothing forced -- content correct, attribution wrong, and a rewrite for attribution is a deep debride nobody asked for.
obs The teaching worth the row: a safety habit attached to COMPOSING a command detaches when the command is recomposed -- the pathspec belongs on every send, retries included. And the day's arc closed a circle: the ledger healed at 15:55 and booked its first red at 16:36, which is exactly what a ledger is for.
